{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The platform's own telemetry puts the driver at the pickup point, not merely in the vicinity: the trace holds 25 consecutive fixes inside the 150 m TRANSPORT_HUB arrival radius recorded in trip_record.pickup_zone_class, far more than the 3 consecutive in-radius fixes POL-NS-02 requires, and that run ends at the cancellation timestamp itself. POL-NS-02 is therefore satisfied and, on that clause's own words, the dispute turns on dwell duration under POL-NS-01 limb (c). Limbs (a) and (d) of POL-NS-01 are also met: there is an 'arrived' event at 07:38:05 and the trip was terminated by the driver with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW, not DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE. The record cannot support the rider's suggestion that no car ever came to the bay.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00209", "EV-TRIP-00209"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver does not dispute the number that defeats the fee, and puts it on the record rather than leaving it to be discovered: the policy-measured dwell is 236 seconds, running from the first qualifying in-geofence fix at 07:44:14 to the cancellation at 07:48:10, which is 64 seconds short of the 300 second minimum for TRANSPORT_HUB, because POL-NS-01(c) runs the clock from that first in-geofence fix and not from the 07:38:05 marker. The recorded wait_time_min of 10.1 is real but is measured from the marker, so the driver does not ask the Judge to charge the fee on the strength of it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00209", "EV-TRIP-00209"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.shortfall_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No false-arrival referral can be entered against this driver. POL-NS-05(ii) fires only where the trip contains no qualifying in-geofence fix anywhere, and this trace carries 25 of them in one continuous run, so whatever view the Judge takes of the 07:38:05 marker under POL-NS-05, the referral limb is unreachable on this record and the driver's record stays clean.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00209", "EV-TRIP-00209"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider cannot reach POL-NS-04, so no rider-side exoneration and no rider-side elimination of coordination fault can be built on it: limb (a) fails at the threshold because not one message in the waiting window is hers — the log holds only the platform's 07:38:06 arrival notice and the driver's two attempts to coordinate. EV-CHAT-00209 is impaired at weight 0.85 with issue UNREAD_MESSAGE (both driver messages and the system notice carry read_at null); that impairment goes only to receipts and not to authorship, so the finding that the rider sent nothing survives the discount, and trip_record.in_app_calls is empty so the voice-call route is closed to her as well.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00209", "EV-TRIP-00209"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.85
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's account that there was no car to be found speaks only to the first minute of the window, not to the last four: from 07:44:14 until the cancellation at 07:48:10 the driver's device was inside the 150 m arrival radius, while the rider's own device was between 50 and 92 metres from the same recorded pickup pin (venue VEN-TAMPINES-INTERCHANGE) across all 88 of her qualifying fixes. For the whole of that 236 second run both devices were inside the hub radii of one recorded pin, so what failed was coordination, not the driver's presence.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00209", "EV-TRIP-00209"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-02", "POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.mean_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The case is decidable and should not be held on an integrity theory. The 07:38:05 marker sits one second from a GPS fix at 07:38:04, far inside the 90 second POL-NS-08(a) allowance; the trace is unbroken at 10 second cadence with no gap of any length; and the SGD 6.00 fare line reconciles with the greater of the TRANSPORT_HUB zone-class fee (6.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (4.00), so no POL-NS-08 limb (a) to (d) defect is present. The deciding dwell rests on weight-1.0 artifacts, so the POL-GEN-02 confidence cap is 1.0.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00209", "EV-TRIP-00209", "EV-FARE-00209"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-08", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.arrived_at",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No abuse or escalation finding is open against the driver: his citable counters are 3 no-show terminations across 88 completed trips in 30 days, a rate of 3.4 percent, below both limbs of the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check (4 or more terminations, and a rate above 8 percent), and rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0 with disputes_with_counterparty_90d 0 on both profiles, so POL-NS-09(c) and (d) are not engaged. No profile field outside the ones POL-NS-07 and POL-NS-09 name — in particular not the lifetime prior_no_show_flags counter — may be used to build an adverse finding against him.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00209", "EV-RPROF-00209"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-NS-09", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver makes no POL-NS-06(i) accumulation argument and asks the Judge to record that he does not: EV-ADVIS-00209-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0, so no traffic_advisory is present to permit separate in-geofence intervals to be summed, and in any event the trace shows a single in-geofence interval with no second interval to add. Advisory relief asserted against a missing artifact would be an abuse of the record and the driver declines it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00209-01", "EV-GPS-00209"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-GEN-02"]
    },
    {
      "text": "If the Judge reads the 369 seconds between the driver's 07:38:05 marker and his first in-geofence fix at 07:44:14 as a hold at the wrong face of the hub — which is the shape of the rider's own account, that she reached the interchange PHV bay at about 07:43 and found no car — then POL-NS-03 governs the driver's money. The trace over that interval is complete (100 percent coverage, no gap), the driver's own in-app message at 07:38:40 placed him at the interchange PHV bay, the trip record shows 2 registered pickup points at VEN-TAMPINES-INTERCHANGE, and neither party named a sub-location in the chat log (the rider sent nothing at all): on those facts POL-NS-03(ii) attributes the mislocation to pin ambiguity rather than to either party, and the driver receives the platform-funded 50 percent goodwill of SGD 3.00 that the fare breakdown already computes under POL-NS-03, independent of and never netted against the rider's full refund.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00209", "EV-TRIP-00209", "EV-FARE-00209", "EV-GPS-00209"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-03", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.dwell_start_offset_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 0.85
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To both parties: the driver's arrival is not in question — the GPS trace places his device inside the 150 m TRANSPORT_HUB arrival radius for 25 consecutive fixes, which satisfies POL-NS-02 — but the fee turns on the dwell, and the dwell falls short. POL-NS-01(c) measures the required 300-second hold from the first qualifying in-geofence GPS fix, not from the 07:38:05 'arrived' tap. The trace puts that first fix at 07:44:14 and the cancellation at 07:48:10: a single continuous hold of 236 seconds, 64 seconds short of the 300-second TRANSPORT_HUB minimum. Limb (c) therefore fails, the SGD 6.00 cancellation fee is not chargeable under POL-NS-01, and POL-NS-06 refunds it in full with no driver compensation payable. The recorded wait_time_min of 10.1 is real but is measured from the marker, which the policy does not accept — the derived offset shows the first in-geofence fix 369 seconds after the marker — and the driver was right not to rest the fee on it. The money: the fare breakdown shows cancellation_fee SGD 6.00, payment_status REFUNDED and refund_issued_sgd SGD 6.00, and 6.00 is exactly the greater of the TRANSPORT_HUB zone-class fee (6.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (4.00), so there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect to disturb it. The SGD 6.00 has already been returned to the rider. Because this dispute was filed by the driver and his claim to restore the fee fails on that arithmetic, POL-GEN-03 gives NO_ACTION: the filing party's claim is not supported and the present state stands — the rider keeps the refund, no sum moves, and both money fields are null. This is the driver-filed case POL-GEN-03 describes, where NO_ACTION leaves the rider refunded and never restores the charge. On the driver's remaining points: I accept that no false-arrival record arises, because POL-NS-05(ii) fires only where the trace contains no qualifying in-geofence fix anywhere and this trace holds 25; and that no escalation is open — the anti-farming check is not met (3 no-show terminations against 88 completed trips in 30 days, 3.4%, below both the count of 4 and the rate of 8%), both disputes_with_counterparty_90d counters are 0, and rider no_show_disputes_30d is 0. On the rider's points: her account of finding no car at the bay is consistent with a first in-radius fix only at 07:44:14, but her own presence does not matter to the refund, since POL-NS-06 refunds whether or not she was there; and her inability to reach POL-NS-04 does not change the outcome. Impairment: the chat log EV-CHAT-00209 is impaired at weight 0.85 with issue UNREAD_MESSAGE (the driver's two messages and the system arrival notice carry read_at null). It is down-weighted and cannot alone support a ruling, but it does not carry the deciding fact — the 236-second dwell comes from EV-GPS-00209 and EV-TRIP-00209, both complete at weight 1.0 — so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0 and I set confidence at 0.95, above the 0.70 floor. No clause produces a referral on these facts."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The driver has no route to accumulate the missing seconds under POL-NS-06(i). That limb sums separate in-geofence intervals only where the trace shows the driver leaving and re-entering, and it is expressly conditioned on a traffic_advisory that is present and populated. The trace shows a single interval - run_count 1, accumulated dwell 236 seconds, identical to the longest run - so there is no second interval to add. The advisory artifact EV-ADVIS-00209-01 is MISSING with weight 0.0 and carries no payload, which makes limb (i) unavailable outright; I rely on that absence itself, which is citable, and I do not assert an advisory that does not exist.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00209-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The driver makes no POL-NS-06(i) accumulation argument and asks the Judge to record that he does not: EV-ADVIS-00209-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0, so no traffic_advisory is present to permit separate in-geofence intervals to be summed, and in any event the trace shows a single in-geofence interval with no second interval to add. Advisory relief asserted against a missing artifact would be an abuse of the record and the driver declines it.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00209-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    },
    {
      "claim": "If the Judge reads the 369 seconds between the driver's 07:38:05 marker and his first in-geofence fix at 07:44:14 as a hold at the wrong face of the hub — which is the shape of the rider's own account, that she reached the interchange PHV bay at about 07:43 and found no car — then POL-NS-03 governs the driver's money. The trace over that interval is complete (100 percent coverage, no gap), the driver's own in-app message at 07:38:40 placed him at the interchange PHV bay, the trip record shows 2 registered pickup points at VEN-TAMPINES-INTERCHANGE, and neither party named a sub-location in the chat log (the rider sent nothing at all): on those facts POL-NS-03(ii) attributes the mislocation to pin ambiguity rather than to either party, and the driver receives the platform-funded 50 percent goodwill of SGD 3.00 that the fare breakdown already computes under POL-NS-03, independent of and never netted against the rider's full refund.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-CHAT-00209 at weight_multiplier 0.85 but does not name its issue code(s): UNREAD_MESSAGE"
    }
  ]
}
